1:0-84 "/// Items, once converted: the domain as `canon infer` and `canon convert` leave it." comment.line.documentation.canon
2:0-3 "///" comment.line.documentation.canon
3:0-85 "/// Today the 6,944 items are rows of Server/Item/propItem.json (127 wire keys), read" comment.line.documentation.canon
4:0-90 "/// in place by resource.vocab for pickers. Converting them takes three steps (CLI §6.4):" comment.line.documentation.canon
5:0-89 "///   1. `canon infer --by dwItemKind1,dwItemKind2` writes the first version of the types" comment.line.documentation.canon
6:0-84 "///      below: one case per kind, one nested case per sub-kind, each allowing every" comment.line.documentation.canon
7:0-43 "///      field its items set (DECISIONS 7);" comment.line.documentation.canon
8:0-57 "///   2. the types are tightened in small reviewed steps;" comment.line.documentation.canon
9:0-87 "///   3. `canon convert items` writes one entry file per item under entries/ (placed by" comment.line.documentation.canon
10:0-45 "///      `@files`) and proves the round trip." comment.line.documentation.canon
11:0-3 "///" comment.line.documentation.canon
12:0-88 "/// This sketch keeps two entries and the cases and fields they, the view and the checks" comment.line.documentation.canon
13:0-85 "/// use. The inferred types cover all 29 (kind1, kind2) pairs found in propItem.json." comment.line.documentation.canon
